    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a fondness for mathematics, especially in physics and biology, where it helps explain the natural world. As a retired teacher, I used math in daily life and enjoyed solving problems. Though I didn’t specialize in it, I found it logical and useful. My master’s degree gave me a solid foundation, and I still appreciate its clarity and structure.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve lived through years of math classes and never felt overwhelmed. My anxiety is low—perhaps because I’ve seen math as a tool, not a challenge. I don’t fear formulas or equations. If I encounter something unfamiliar, I take a deep breath and try to break it down. My calm nature helps me stay steady, even when numbers seem complex.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I didn’t use AI for math learning recently. I’ve been retired and don’t have daily academic needs. However, I’ve used simple apps to check facts or solve puzzles. I found them helpful for quick reference, but I prefer traditional methods. AI feels like a tool, not a replacement for understanding. I remain cautious about over-reliance on technology.",
